Description: PaperWM-style scrolling tiling for Pantheon
 A Gala plugin: each workspace on the primary monitor becomes a horizontal
 strip of columns that scrolls to follow focus, keeping Wingpanel, the dock
 and the multitasking view. Super+arrows move focus, Super+Shift+arrows move
 windows, Super+R cycles a column's width.
 .
 A Wingpanel indicator toggles tiling for the workspace and the focused
 window, and a "Tiling" page in System Settings (Personal) sets the gap,
 column widths, per-app rules and shows the shortcuts.
 .
 It moves some of Pantheon's default keys to make room: workspace switching
 goes to Ctrl+Super+Left/Right (in place of half-screen tiling, which is
 turned off with edge tiling), the multitasking view keeps Super+S only, and
 move-to-monitor is unbound. Values set in a user's own settings still win.
 Gala loads plugins at startup, so log out and back in after installing.
